{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>A woman when she yields seed and gives birth to a male.</b> They have already said: 'A woman who emits seed first gives birth to a male' (Niddah 31a). This is because the woman's seed — that is, the moisture emitted from her during intercourse — does not enter into the formation of a male at all; rather, her blood is acted upon and coagulates by the man's seed. And when her seminal moisture enters into her coagulated blood, it constitutes superfluous moisture, and the offspring will be female." "<b>As in the days of the impurity of her sickness.</b> For during the first seven days she discharges menstrual blood that has not yet putrefied and has not lost the form of its impurity."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "The phrase זרע האשה is rendered 'the woman's seed' following Sforno's own gloss הוא הלחות הנפלט ממנה, identifying it with the moisture emitted from her."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:07.614461934Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}